Manifest files **have** to go in `<head>` or Chrome doesn't see it. Currently this can get caught in RSC and your manifest link can end up a thousand lines down in your `<body>` and Chrome (on desktop and mobile) just misses it.

So `manifest.ts` and the manifest config object are just straight up completely broken for anyone using RSC rn.

For anyone else running into this headache, just put your manifest link directly in the `<head>` tag in your root `layout.tsx`.

```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <head>
        <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json" />
      </head>
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

