Dynamic matcher in middleware / proxy – any workaround?
### Summary

According to the [docs](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/file-conventions/proxy#matcher), the matcher config must be statically analyzable at build time:
>The matcher values need to be constants so they can be statically analyzed at build-time. Dynamic values such as variables will be ignored.

This blocks use cases like runtime maintenance mode, where I’d want something like:

```tsx
export const config: ProxyConfig = {
  matcher: isMaintenanceModeEnabled
    ? ["/:path*"]
    : ["/login", "/verify-otp", "/signup", "/user/:path*"],
};
```

Current workaround (inside proxy)
This works functionally, but it still forces all requests through the proxy, which introduces unnecessary overhead even when the logic short-circuits early.

```tsx
